1:1-1 (* EXPECT-ERROR: an allocation in pool scratch escapes its pool *)
2:1-14 (* The storage of a local pool is answered through a CALLEE.  It was\n   observed 2026-10-07 writing RdfTest.  A helper read a document's\n   octets with `RETURN DynStr.Utf8 (p, text)', p its own scratch pool,\n   and the checker accepted it.  It followed a RETURN of a NEW in a\n   local pool and of a view into one, not of a call that answers INTO\n   the pool it is handed.  The test then refused every hand document as\n   "not UTF-8": the octets were freed before the caller read them.  A\n   pool parameter is a promise that the answer lives there\n   (docs/pools.md, "the pool parameter appears exactly when the\n   allocation outlives the call").  A checker that does not read the\n   promise lets the frame die under the answer.  Utf8 went with the\n   CHAR builder at the switch (2026-10-31); Bytes answers into the\n   pool it is handed in the same way. *)
comments=2
